HST Office: ribbon key tips for the reworked tabs; Help is Y; menu buttons and input fields.

From the ribbon UX audit of 13/11/2026 (section 8.3):
- the commands the reworked tabs put on the ribbon get the letters people know from the familiar office
  suite: Sheets Home Merge M, Wrap Text W, Percent P, Currency AN, alignment AL/AC/AR, Conditional
  Formatting L; Find FD and Replace R in the Editing groups; the citation, page, table and slide commands;
- a ribbon menu button ("Chèn ▾", "Sắp xếp và lọc ▾", "Lề ▾") can have a letter of its own, looked up by
  its widget id (the part before ":Menu ..."); before, such buttons always got a generated letter;
- the Help tab is Y instead of Y2;
- the tip of an input field (font name, size) hangs below the field instead of over its lower half,
  where the field covered it.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
